DSH-Android patch 22: llm-service-lite (vendored @snnh/dsh-llm-service-lite 0.2.1), a profile's
reasoning declaration replaces the family table's. Applies on top of 14, 16, 17, 18.

The app lets the user declare a model's reasoning control (provider editor → 推理控制, #46) for ids
the family table does not know or misreads. Upstream `resolveModel` took each of `effort` and
`thinking` from the family when the profile's list was empty (the config schema materializes an
absent list as `[]`), kept the family's effort levels (which win over thinking modes) when the
profile declared `thinking` only, and kept the family's default level whenever `effort` was empty.
So neither "a thinking switch" nor "no reasoning control" could be declared for an id whose family
has effort levels. Now a profile that declares effort levels, thinking modes or a `thinkingStyle`
states the whole control: its own lists (empty ones included) and no family default level; a style
with no levels means no control. A profile that declares none of the three inherits the family's
levels and default, as before.

